1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,036
A gas flame heats milk.

2
00:00:02,036 --> 00:00:04,733
A cold pack turns icy when you squeeze it.

3
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:07,224
Pulling a Lego tower apart takes effort.

4
00:00:07,624 --> 00:00:09,960
Every change has its own heat story.

5
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,242
Diya lights the gas stove.

6
00:00:12,242 --> 00:00:14,222
Cooking gas is mostly butane.

7
00:00:14,572 --> 00:00:18,063
One mole of it burns and gives out
two thousand six hundred fifty eight

8
00:00:18,063 --> 00:00:18,963
kilojoules.

9
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:23,304
By the end, you will know five kinds
of enthalpy change, and how to find

10
00:00:23,304 --> 00:00:25,109
a reaction's heat from a table.

11
00:00:25,759 --> 00:00:27,726
First, a fair way to compare.

12
00:00:27,726 --> 00:00:30,958
Like runners on the same
track, in the same weather.

13
00:00:31,308 --> 00:00:35,874
Each substance pure, at one bar,
usually at two ninety eight kelvin.

14
00:00:35,874 --> 00:00:37,772
This is the standard state.

15
00:00:38,122 --> 00:00:41,986
The heat change then is the
standard enthalpy of reaction.

16
00:00:41,986 --> 00:00:44,201
The small circle means standard.

17
00:00:44,601 --> 00:00:47,329
On our molecule bench, the first kind.

18
00:00:47,329 --> 00:00:48,892
Enthalpy of formation.

19
00:00:49,242 --> 00:00:53,115
Formation means building one mole of
a compound from its elements, like

20
00:00:53,115 --> 00:00:54,824
one house from loose bricks.

21
00:00:55,224 --> 00:00:58,381
Hydrogen gas, and half
a mole of oxygen gas.

22
00:00:58,381 --> 00:01:01,058
Their bonds open, and the atoms join.

23
00:01:01,458 --> 00:01:04,078
Liquid water forms, and heat comes out.

24
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:05,262
Down the ladder.

25
00:01:05,662 --> 00:01:08,857
Minus two eighty five point
eight kilojoules per mole.

26
00:01:08,857 --> 00:01:11,018
The enthalpy of formation of water.

27
00:01:11,518 --> 00:01:16,478
An element in its normal form, like
oxygen gas or graphite, has zero.

28
00:01:16,478 --> 00:01:18,153
Nothing needs building.

29
00:01:18,803 --> 00:01:20,111
Now the opposite.

30
00:01:20,111 --> 00:01:22,838
Pull a molecule apart into single atoms.

31
00:01:22,838 --> 00:01:24,299
This is atomization.

32
00:01:24,649 --> 00:01:27,297
Here is methane, one carbon
holding four hydrogens.

33
00:01:27,697 --> 00:01:28,597
Snap.

34
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:29,267
One bond breaks.

35
00:01:29,267 --> 00:01:30,565
Snap, snap, snap.

36
00:01:30,565 --> 00:01:32,232
Each break needs energy in.

37
00:01:32,632 --> 00:01:36,516
One thousand six hundred sixty
five kilojoules per mole went in.

38
00:01:36,516 --> 00:01:38,935
The enthalpy of atomization of methane.

39
00:01:39,335 --> 00:01:41,419
Share it between four bonds.

40
00:01:41,419 --> 00:01:43,226
About four sixteen each.

41
00:01:43,226 --> 00:01:45,321
The mean CH bond enthalpy.

42
00:01:45,721 --> 00:01:50,325
Bond enthalpy: energy to break
one mole of a bond, in gases.

43
00:01:50,325 --> 00:01:52,257
HH, four thirty five.

44
00:01:52,907 --> 00:01:54,988
Two more members of the family.

45
00:01:55,338 --> 00:01:58,326
Combustion: burning one
mole fully in oxygen.

46
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,858
Butane, minus twenty six fifty eight.

47
00:02:00,858 --> 00:02:03,291
Glucose, minus twenty eight oh two.

48
00:02:03,691 --> 00:02:06,749
Solution: dissolving one
mole, like salt in water.

49
00:02:06,749 --> 00:02:09,584
Breaking the crystal takes
seven eighty eight in.

50
00:02:09,984 --> 00:02:11,745
Water molecules hug each ion.

51
00:02:11,745 --> 00:02:12,916
This is hydration.

52
00:02:12,916 --> 00:02:14,317
Seven eighty four out.

53
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:17,187
So salt dissolves for only plus four.

54
00:02:17,187 --> 00:02:21,677
For ISC, neutralisation: about
fifty seven out per mole of water.

55
00:02:22,277 --> 00:02:23,728
Now a tricky pair.

56
00:02:23,728 --> 00:02:28,226
Nitrogen plus three hydrogen gives
two ammonia, minus ninety two point

57
00:02:28,226 --> 00:02:29,126
four.

58
00:02:29,211 --> 00:02:32,249
But formation always
counts one mole of product.

59
00:02:32,649 --> 00:02:33,867
Pause and think.

60
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:38,196
Is minus ninety two point four the
enthalpy of formation of ammonia?

61
00:02:41,396 --> 00:02:42,296
No!

62
00:02:41,811 --> 00:02:43,660
That equation makes two moles.

63
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:44,560
Halve it.

64
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:48,252
The enthalpy of formation of ammonia
is minus forty six point two.

65
00:02:48,902 --> 00:02:51,892
Now the most useful rule, step by step.

66
00:02:52,242 --> 00:02:53,142
Step one.

67
00:02:52,863 --> 00:02:54,763
Pull the reactants back into elements.

68
00:02:54,763 --> 00:02:56,466
That flips their formation values.

69
00:02:57,216 --> 00:02:58,116
Step two.

70
00:02:57,851 --> 00:02:59,830
Build the products from those elements.

71
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:01,531
That adds their formation values.

72
00:03:02,281 --> 00:03:03,181
Step three.

73
00:03:02,939 --> 00:03:05,643
So, products minus reactants,
each times its coefficient.

74
00:03:06,393 --> 00:03:07,293
Example.

75
00:03:07,124 --> 00:03:10,179
Limestone breaks into
lime and carbon dioxide.

76
00:03:10,929 --> 00:03:15,712
Minus six thirty five point one, minus
three ninety three point five, plus

77
00:03:15,712 --> 00:03:17,532
twelve oh six point nine.

78
00:03:17,532 --> 00:03:19,918
Plus one seventy eight point three.

79
00:03:19,918 --> 00:03:21,010
Heat goes in.

80
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:22,660
Remember this.

81
00:03:22,499 --> 00:03:24,434
Formation values:
products minus reactants.

82
00:03:24,434 --> 00:03:26,334
Bond enthalpies: reactants minus products.

83
00:03:27,034 --> 00:03:28,725
Now, one worked example.

84
00:03:29,025 --> 00:03:32,116
Hydrogen and chlorine make
two hydrogen chloride.

85
00:03:32,116 --> 00:03:37,180
Bond enthalpies: HH four thirty five,
Cl Cl two forty two, H Cl four thirty

86
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:38,080
one.

87
00:03:38,186 --> 00:03:39,212
Bonds broken.

88
00:03:39,212 --> 00:03:41,696
Four thirty five plus two forty two.

89
00:03:41,696 --> 00:03:43,245
Six seventy seven in.

90
00:03:43,995 --> 00:03:44,895
Bonds made.

91
00:03:44,872 --> 00:03:46,634
Two times four thirty one.

92
00:03:46,634 --> 00:03:48,054
Eight sixty two out.

93
00:03:48,804 --> 00:03:51,340
Six seventy seven minus eight sixty two.

94
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:53,429
Minus one eighty five kilojoules.

95
00:03:54,179 --> 00:03:56,040
More comes out than goes in.

96
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,327
Heat is given out.

97
00:03:57,977 --> 00:03:59,439
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:03:59,789 --> 00:04:02,333
Some students use products minus
reactants with bond enthalpies.

99
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,679
They get plus one eighty five.

100
00:04:04,079 --> 00:04:07,086
But breaking takes energy
in, and making gives it out.

101
00:04:07,086 --> 00:04:08,471
Reactants minus products.

102
00:04:08,471 --> 00:04:09,781
Minus one eighty five.

103
00:04:10,431 --> 00:04:11,693
Where is this asked?

104
00:04:11,693 --> 00:04:13,251
Boards ask the definitions.

105
00:04:13,251 --> 00:04:16,385
Entrance tests give a table
and ask a reaction's enthalpy.

106
00:04:16,985 --> 00:04:18,194
Exam level now.

107
00:04:18,194 --> 00:04:22,968
Formation values: carbon dioxide minus
three ninety three point five, water

108
00:04:22,968 --> 00:04:27,854
minus two eighty five point eight,
methane minus seventy four point eight.

109
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:30,313
Find methane's enthalpy of combustion.

110
00:04:30,313 --> 00:04:31,573
Pause and solve.

111
00:04:36,973 --> 00:04:38,063
The answer is B.

112
00:04:38,063 --> 00:04:40,837
Minus eight ninety point
three kilojoules per mole.

113
00:04:41,337 --> 00:04:45,943
Methane plus two oxygen gives
carbon dioxide plus two water.

114
00:04:45,943 --> 00:04:47,355
Oxygen is zero.

115
00:04:47,855 --> 00:04:48,755
Products.

116
00:04:48,547 --> 00:04:52,713
Minus three ninety three point five,
plus two times minus two eighty five

117
00:04:52,713 --> 00:04:53,613
point eight.

118
00:04:53,595 --> 00:04:55,606
Minus nine sixty five point one.

119
00:04:56,106 --> 00:04:57,426
Minus the reactants.

120
00:04:57,426 --> 00:05:01,268
Minus nine sixty five point one,
plus seventy four point eight.

121
00:05:01,268 --> 00:05:03,207
Minus eight ninety point three.

122
00:05:03,207 --> 00:05:04,445
A forgot the two.

123
00:05:05,045 --> 00:05:06,585
Here is your recap.

124
00:05:06,585 --> 00:05:08,168
Screenshot this card.

125
00:05:11,368 --> 00:05:13,554
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

126
00:05:13,954 --> 00:05:14,854
One.

127
00:05:14,472 --> 00:05:17,978
Why is the enthalpy of
formation of oxygen gas zero?

128
00:05:18,778 --> 00:05:19,678
Two.

129
00:05:19,179 --> 00:05:21,522
Why does dissolving salt
take so little heat?

130
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,222
Three.

131
00:05:22,711 --> 00:05:25,096
With bond enthalpies, why is
it reactants minus products?

132
00:05:25,996 --> 00:05:29,256
Next time: can you find a reaction's
heat without ever doing it?

133
00:05:29,256 --> 00:05:30,693
We find out in Hess's law.
